\textbf{Majority-action floor.} An always-EDUCATIONAL, flat-bid policy on the SEARCH channel achieves 35.1\% match and -\$15.38 profit -- better than the random baseline (21.6\%, -\$170.03) but still negative. Context-aware agents dominate it. This retires the ``engineered strawman'' objection.

\textbf{Matched-family ablation.} Nearest-centroid on intent-only (\Ag{cc_intent_only}, 1 signal, fitted) achieves 72.7\% match and +\$102.28. The 3-signal NCC (\Ag{am_multisignal}, 98.9\%, +\$206.13, hand-set generative centroids) outperforms by +\$103.85 (\pv{5.16\!\times\!10^{-46}}, paired bootstrap CI +\$100.13..+\$107.55). The learned-vs-learned comparison gives +\$50.01 (\pv{8.5\!\times\!10^{-32}}, d$_z$=3.96). Both gaps are signal-driven, not classifier-capacity-driven (same NCC family).

